{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",

  // T7-W6. `project` was `src/**` alone for two campaigns, so `scripts/**` and the NON-SPEC
  // half of `e2e/` sat outside the census entirely — which is how `e2e/magnitude-reporter.mjs`
  // (zero referents, retired here) and `scripts/check-theme-tokens.mjs` (no lane runs it)
  // survived a `files: "error"` rule. A dead-file rule that cannot see two of the three
  // first-party source dirs is not a dead-file rule. Widened to both.
  //
  // `perf-rig/**` stays OUT, deliberately and on the record — and the rationale is RE-DERIVED
  // FROM DISK here (T9-W6 §6.1; the T7-W6 wording carried a false count and a false
  // instrument, banked at evidence/w6/kills-census/k-knip-perfrig-trued.txt).
  //
  // WHAT IS TRUE. Nothing in the rig imports anything else in the rig: every ES import across
  // its EIGHT `.mjs` modules is a `node:` builtin or the `playwright` package, zero relative
  // specifiers. They reach each other as CHILD PROCESSES — nine `.sh` drivers spawning `node
  // <module>` and each other (`rounds.sh` → `matrix.sh` → `run-safari.sh`; `sim-matrix.sh` →
  // `run-sim.sh`; `cpu-attrib.sh`, `pw-driver.sh`, `w5-bench.sh`, `w5-solve-trim.sh`),
  // `ci-subset.mjs` spawning its own build and probe server, and the hand invocations
  // `perf-rig/README.md` documents. `probe.js` is a tenth file that is neither: it is injected
  // into the page. A module graph cannot see one edge of that, so the widening would buy eight
  // false reds instead of one true one.
  //
  // WHAT THE OLD WORDING GOT WRONG, named so the next reader does not inherit it: it said SIX
  // modules (there are eight `.mjs`, plus `probe.js`, plus nine `.sh`), it named `run-safari.sh`
  // and `run-sim.sh` as the callers (they are two of nine), and it handed the rig's membership
  // question to `scripts/check-lane-membership.mjs` "which reads ci.yml, where the rig's
  // callers live". That gate does not scope `perf-rig/**` at all, and ci.yml has carried ZERO
  // `perf-rig` references since O-12 deleted the perf lane at `d1daefb3`. The rig is a LOCAL
  // instrument whole — LEDGER CH-53, restamped T9-W0 — and that, not a gate, is the answer to
  // its membership question.
  //
  // `../relay/*.ts` JOINS THE CENSUS AT T9-W6 §6.2. The relay is a DEPLOYED artifact — one
  // Worker, one Durable Object, shipped by the same gate that ships the SPA — and it sat
  // outside every static gate this package runs because it is a sibling directory with no
  // package.json of its own (wrangler.toml's header says why: it borrows this package's
  // wrangler and vitest, so it needs neither a manifest nor a node_modules). Sibling or not,
  // the module graph reaches it fine, and a dead module over there is the same defect as a
  // dead module here. The glob is flat (`*.ts`, not `**/*.ts`) because the directory is flat:
  // two source files, and `.wrangler/` + `node_modules/` beside them carry only build cache.
  "project": [
    "src/**/*.{ts,vue,css}",
    "scripts/**/*.mjs",
    "e2e/**/*.{ts,mjs}",
    "../relay/*.ts"
  ],

  // Roots whose CALLER is not JavaScript, so no module graph can reach them. Each is named
  // here with the caller that runs it — a file listed without one is a hole.
  //   scripts/dist-identity.mjs      .github/workflows/ci.yml, the dist lane (T9-W5 §5.3):
  //                                  `run: node scripts/dist-identity.mjs --self-test` and
  //                                  `--dist dist`; perf-rig/run-safari.sh + run-sim.sh reach
  //                                  the same file through the AUDIT prepend.
  //   ../relay/relay.ts              web/relay/wrangler.toml, `main = "relay.ts"` — the
  //                                  Worker's entry, loaded by wrangler and by nothing in any
  //                                  module graph. It ships through
  //                                  ../../scripts/deploy-gated.sh, which is the only thing
  //                                  authorised to run `wrangler deploy` (T9-W5 §5.1).
  //   ../relay/relay.test.ts         scripts.test:unit:relay in this package.json —
  //                                  `vitest run --root ../relay`, collected by glob from a
  //                                  root outside this one, which is the same species of
  //                                  unreachable-by-graph the playwright block below handles
  //                                  for `e2e/**/*.spec.ts`.
  // WHAT THIS PAIR DOES *NOT* BUY, said plainly rather than left to be assumed: knip does not
  // grade unused EXPORTS on an entry file, so `relay.ts`'s exported surface is not under the
  // exports rule the way `src/**` is. Both files are entries because both really are reached
  // by a non-JS caller; the alternative (make the test the only entry and let it pull
  // `relay.ts` in) does not work — knip reports `../relay/relay.ts` unused under it, measured
  // at evidence/w6/gates-relay/knip-widen-probe-1-testfile-orphan.txt. What the pair DOES buy
  // is the dead-FILE law over the relay directory, proven by plant at
  // evidence/w6/gates-relay/knip-plant-RED.txt.
  // `e2e/ch62-admission.ts` USED to sit here too, cited to ".github/workflows/ch62-probe.yml,
  // the CH-62 admission arm" — and that workflow never imported it. It named the module in two
  // prose comments and wrote a same-named JSON artifact; the `entry` line was the only thing
  // in the estate claiming the file was reachable, so knip answered yes on the author's word
  // for a 4,239 B module with zero callers. Both died at T9-W6 §6.1, together with the
  // workflow, which was `workflow_dispatch`-only for a chronic RETIRED at T8 formation.
  // `scripts/golden-magnitude.mjs` USED to sit here, cited to "ci.yml, the golden lane" — a
  // lane deleted at T7-WGATE on standing ruling O-12 (d1daefb3). The entry outlived its
  // caller by a whole campaign, which is how a dead file keeps a live-looking badge: knip
  // asks "is it reachable", and an `entry` line answers yes on the author's word. T9-W5 §5.4
  // adjudicated the file KEPT as a declared local instrument, so its caller is now
  // `scripts.test:golden:magnitude` in package.json — a real referent knip resolves for
  // itself — and it carries a `NOT-A-LANE:` header that check-lane-membership.mjs polices.
  // NOT a place to park an unwired gate: a `check-*.mjs` belongs to a lane or declares
  // NOT-A-LANE in its own header, and check-lane-membership.mjs reds if it does neither.
  "entry": ["scripts/dist-identity.mjs", "../relay/relay.ts", "../relay/relay.test.ts"],

  "ignore": ["src/games/shared/scene.css", "src/games/shared/gameCell.css"],

  // `make` is reached through scripts.wasm (`make -C ../../csp-solver/wasm wasm`).
  "ignoreBinaries": ["make"],

  // Dependencies whose CONSUMER is outside this package, named with that consumer — the
  // same law the `entry` block keeps for files.
  //   wrangler  ../../scripts/deploy-gated.sh, which carries BOTH deploy lines (Pages
  //             and the relay Worker) and reaches the binary through
  //             node_modules/.bin. web/relay borrows the same install
  //             (web/relay/wrangler.toml names the path). The line sat in
  //             `scripts.deploy:raw` from T5-W6.2 purely so knip could see the binary
  //             consumed, and that appeasement was an ungated side door: `npm run
  //             deploy:raw` shipped `dist/` past every refusal in the gate (T9-W5,
  //             V3-C6). The gate is the consumer; this is where knip is told so.
  "ignoreDependencies": ["wrangler"],
  "playwright": {
    "config": ["playwright.config.ts"],
    "entry": ["e2e/**/*.spec.ts"]
  },
  "rules": {
    "files": "error",
    "dependencies": "error",
    "devDependencies": "error",
    "optionalPeerDependencies": "error",
    "unlisted": "error",
    "binaries": "error",
    "unresolved": "error",
    "duplicates": "error",
    "exports": "error",
    "nsExports": "error",
    "types": "error",
    "nsTypes": "error",
    "enumMembers": "error"
  }
}
